    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe membership level is computed in `OwnerMapper` when mapping an `Owner` to `OwnerDto`. Previously it was an inline expression hard-capped at 3:\n\n```java\nMath.min(3, 1 + email? + namesake0?)\n```\n\nI introduced a dedicated helper `MembershipLevel` (matching the existing `AgeBand`/`CustomerCode` helper pattern so MapStruct doesn't treat it as a mapping method) and pointed the `@Mapping` expression at it.\n\n**New logic** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/MembershipLevel.java`):\n- Base level 1, plus one point each for an email, a `namesakeCount` of 0, and a household of 3+ members \u2014 these pre-tenure factors reach at most level 3.\n- Level 4 additionally requires **tenure of more than 365 days** since `registrationDate`. The cap is 4 only when `tenureDays > 365`, otherwise 3.\n\nSince a newly created owner registers today, its tenure is 0, so the cap stays at 3 \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0 and a 3-member household lands at level 3, not 4, exactly as specified.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` passes and the full `./mvnw test` run is green.",
